  "answer": "Sales should use the **Corpus Readiness Checklist** shared during discovery and contracting, per [NL-015#NL-015-S04] and [NL-023#NL-023-S07]. This checklist must flag scanned, image-only PDFs and OCR requirements, because without a text layer, citation accuracy drops and the go-live quality checks fail [NL-015#NL-015-S04]. A mandatory pre-onboarding format audit of a 20-core-document sample should be required during sales discovery; if scanned PDFs are detected, the sales team must flag it early so CS can adjust the target timeline [NL-031#NL-031-S06]. This directly supports the standard Enterprise implementation timeline of 8–10 weeks (or the historical median of 8.7 weeks) [NL-031#NL-031-S02], and sales should not promise a shorter rollout (e.g., 4–6 weeks) when these blockers exist [NL-015#NL-015-S04]. Additionally, per the sales playbook, before promising deployment dates, sales must consult other departments for custom SLAs/data deletion (Priya Raman, Security Policy NL-007), pricing changes (Marcus Reed, NL-003), and product roadmap dates (Sofia Almeida, NL-014) — and must frame roadmap dates as targets, not guarantees [NL-009#NL-009-S08].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
